body:
@mkouba: We have 4-5 git repositories with a multi maven project inside each.
They all define beans and use jindex to help the discovery. 

One of the repositories contains the runnable jars, they have the quarkus-maven-plugin and they build the application. 

We build eigher using a pom adding all repos into one maven reactor or build the projects one by one and then as the last step the runnables. It does not matter which one is used the issue can be reproduced on that machine which more powerful CPU.

@manovotn:
Only one of the beans gets the startup notification.

It seems that in the bad case ReadModelComponent_Observer is called first, and then BatchedDBReadModelComponent_Observer. In the good case only the second.

**SendEventHandlerWorker** is extending **BatchedDBReadModelComponent** which is extending **ReadModelComponent**!

Both BatchedDBReadModelComponent and ReadModelComponent are base classes, but they are not declared abstract.

Readmodel:
    public void onStart(@Observes StartupEvent ev) {
        log.info("Subscribed {} to {}", getReadModelName() + "@" + System.identityHashCode(this), topic);
    }

Batched:
    @Override
    public void onStart(@Observes StartupEvent ev) {
        manager.load(this);
        super.onStart(ev);
    }
